            "subfield": {
              "code": "a",
              "content": "Area: From portions north of Francis and Dight Streets to \"Agricultural College Farm\" in the south, from Edward Luttrell's 400 acre grant \"Hobartville\" in the west to the general cemetery and Richmond Permanent Common in the east."
            },
            "tag": 500
          },
          {
            "ind2": " ",
            "ind1": " ",
            "subfield": {
              "code": "a",
              "content": "Shows measured, numbered allotments and portions, named streets,  landowners' names, reserves (for public recreation, temporary common, public school purposes, rail purposes, water, public pound), churches, cemeteries, railway line, railway station, Richmond Permanent Common, Hobartville [Estate], \"Agricultural College Farm\", Pugh's Lagoon."
            },
            "tag": 500
          },
          {
            "ind2": " ",
            "ind1": " ",
            "subfield": {
              "code": "a",
              "content": "National Library of Australia's copy has handwritten annotations in pencil \"Richmond land use 1952\". Annotations show farming lands north of Francis Street, aerodrome east of Hobart Street, school on Burgess Street, health centre, hall and library on Market Street, ice works on Dight Street, and a factory on Windsor Street."
            },
            "tag": 500
          },
